            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> 3\\. Virtual text should merely provide a quick hint. If you wanted to see everything, you should use `vim.lsp.diagnostic.show_line_diagnostics()` instead.\n>     The current approach is simple and works. If you wanted to wrap, you would run into tons of problems like what about two subsequent lines having long diagnostics? What about wrapping the virtual text, but the next line fills out all of `&tw` already?\n>     As long as we can't add full virtual lines (lines between actual lines), I'd prefer the current simple approach.\n\nThis appears to be deprecated. Use `vim.diagnostic.open_float()` instead. Also the popup wont show unless you are focused on the line with the error so set a keybind to toggle it or sth \n\n```\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Leader>tf\", function()\n\tvim.diagnostic.open_float()\nend)\n```",
